# Agile Workflow – Comic: "Why I Should Graduate from BRICS University"

This Agile plan breaks down the comic creation into focused 10-minute sprints, including a final review sprint to refine and reflect before publishing.

---

## Sprint 1: Pre-production – Script & Planning  
**Duration:** 10 minutes  
**Goal:** Define the comic concept, script, characters, and visual layout.

### Tasks:
- [ ] Finalize comic theme and title
- [ ] Write panel-by-panel script with dialogue
- [ ] Sketch quick thumbnail layout of 4–5 panels
- [ ] Identify main character(s) and setting

**Deliverable:**  
- Rapid script + thumbnail storyboard for the comic

---

## Sprint 2: Rough Art – Layout & Composition  
**Duration:** 10 minutes  
**Goal:** Establish visual flow and panel structure.

### Tasks:
- [ ] Create fast rough sketches for all panels
- [ ] Place rough speech bubbles/dialogue
- [ ] Define character poses and panel layout
- [ ] Prioritize storytelling over detail

**Deliverable:**  
- Complete rough sketch layout with text placement

---

## Sprint 3: Line Art & Lettering  
**Duration:** 10 minutes  
**Goal:** Finalize strong linework and clean up text.

### Tasks:
- [ ] Ink all panels with bold, readable lines
- [ ] Add final speech bubbles and dialogue
- [ ] Clean up composition if needed

**Deliverable:**  
- Black-and-white final draft with readable dialogue

---

## Sprint 4: Coloring & Publishing  
**Duration:** 10 minutes  
**Goal:** Add color polish and prepare to share.

### Tasks:
- [ ] Apply flat color quickly to all panels
- [ ] Add light shading or highlights
- [ ] Export final version (PNG or PDF)
- [ ] Prepare to publish

**Deliverable:**  
- Final colored and exported version of the comic

---

## Sprint 5: Review & Polish  
**Duration:** 10 minutes  
**Goal:** Reflect on the process and improve clarity or details.

### Tasks:
- [ ] Re-read all dialogue and check flow
- [ ] Fix any awkward poses or framing
- [ ] Adjust color balance or contrast
- [ ] Review final export format (web/social/print)
- [ ] Make notes for future comics or improvements

**Deliverable:**  
- Clean, polished, and reviewed version of the comic, ready to publish or present

---

## Tools & Boards  
- **Task Board Columns:** `To Do | In Progress | Review | Done`  
- **Suggested Tools:** Trello, Notion, Figma, Krita, Clip Studio Paint, GitHub Projects

---

## Sprint Retrospectives (Optional)  
After each sprint, reflect with:
- What worked well?
- What could be improved?
- Should I iterate more or move on?

---

## Final Result  
A complete 4–5 panel comic delivered using rapid Agile methods — showcasing creativity, structure, and self-review in a lean workflow.
